  "Question": "A class has the following blood types: 20 students with type A, 15 with type B, 10 with type O, and 5 with type AB. If a student is selected at random, what is the probability that the student has type O blood? (Express the result as a fraction in simplest form.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1/5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "There are \\(20+15+10+5=50\\) students in the class, of whom 10 have type O blood. The probability is \\(10/50=1/5\\).",
